xv6 is a re-implementation of Dennis Ritchie's and Ken Thompson's Unix
Version 6 (v6).  xv6 loosely follows the structure and style of v6,
but is implemented for a 64-bit LoongArch multiprocessor, targeting
QEMU's "virt" machine, using ANSI C.

ACKNOWLEDGMENTS

See README.common at the top of this repository for the acknowledgments
shared by every port here - John Lions's Commentary, the contributor
list, and the copyright.  What follows is specific to this port.

BUILDING AND RUNNING XV6

From the repository root: run ./configure once (it detects a
loongarch64 cross toolchain and a qemu-system-loongarch64 on this
machine), then `make build-loongarch`, `make run-loongarch`
(interactive shell under QEMU), or `make test-loongarch` (boots
headless and runs the usertests suite).
